" =============================================================================
" 07-marks.vifm -- marks, bookmarks and per-directory behaviour
" =============================================================================
"
" Jump to a mark with 'x (e.g. 'h for home). :marks lists them all.
" These point only at directories that actually exist on this machine.

mark h ~/
mark c ~/.config/
mark d ~/Downloads/
mark D ~/Documents/
mark p ~/Pictures/
mark m ~/Music/
mark V ~/Videos/
mark l ~/Laboratory/
mark z ~/Zotero/
mark t /tmp/
mark v ~/.config/vifm/

" ------------------------------------------------------------- autocommands
" DirEnter patterns without a slash match the last path component anywhere;
" patterns with slashes match the whole path. 'sort' and 'lsview' are local
" options, so these settings stay attached to the pane that entered the
" directory and do not leak into the other one.

" Downloads is a queue, not a library: newest first.
autocmd DirEnter ~/Downloads set sort=-mtime

" Image directories are much easier to scan as a grid of names.
autocmd DirEnter ~/Pictures/** set lsview
autocmd DirEnter !~/Pictures/** set nolsview

" This config tree is browsed on a narrow pane more often than not, and the
" file names here are long; drop the mtime column while inside it.
autocmd DirEnter ~/.config/vifm/** set viewcolumns=-{name}..,8{size}

" Inside a .git directory the interesting thing is almost always a dotfile.
autocmd DirEnter **/.git/** set dotfiles
